  "notes": "1970s-rock and new-wave-inflected pop whose defining researched fact is the tracking method, not a pattern: the kit was \"recorded as a real kit in a domestic room (the drum kit was set up in a TV room with the furniture removed) — so the grammar is a played 8th- or 16th-note groove with room ambience and no grid-quantised hats\". That is authored as the loosest humanize block in this batch — `quantizeStrength` 0.72 with real per-lane jitter — plus `snare.reverb` large, a wide velocity spread and `hihat.continuous` true with no roll vocabulary at all. \"Tambourine and shaker double the backbeat\" is the perc lane list at `downbeat` placement. The low end is explicitly not an 808: \"melodic electric bass playing a running 8th-note line that outlines the chord tones is the main countermelody; on the funk-facing records the bass carries the hook\", so the bassline is `independent_riff` at a low `followRootsProb` with the widest passing-tone set here, and no `drums.bass808` block is authored. Harmony is \"diatonic 4-bar loops with the chord rhythm on the beat and an arpeggiated synth or guitar figure over the top\" plus \"a bright major with a flattened-7th borrow\", which is the mixolydian weight and the VII family. Melody is \"mid-register and conversational with a narrow chorus leap; harmonies are close and few\", so `octaveJumpProb` stays low and the counter density is modest. Arrangement encodes the documented short runtime. ⚠ Every BPM bound is a number the entry itself states and nothing else: \"BPM 100—175; the guitar-synth-pop mode reads ~174 which is best modelled as ~87 with a driven 8th-note pulse [LOW-CONF]\". So the floor is that folded ~87 and the ceiling is the entry's own stated 175; the entry names no tempo between 100 and 174, so the band's edges are quoted and its interior is not. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the key list and `bpm.mode` 100, which is the stated band floor chosen as the centre of gravity rather than a reading. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium and says the tempo/key band is inferred from catalogue convention, and its own [LOW-CONF] mark on the folded tempo is repeated here.",
